      "writtenOn": "2019-07-08T08:02:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "IIUC, APEXes can use shared libraries from other APEXes implicitly (If libfoo.so in APEX A has a stable C interface and other APEX B depends on libfoo.so, then libfoo.so is shared between A and B.) I think that the dependency can be explicit via \"uses\" property. So, even if the common APEX provides libc++.so, other APEX can choose not to use the common libc++.so by not setting \"uses\". \n\nDo you think this will conflict with the current behavior or this is somewhat away from the original APEX ideas?",
